From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 012/138] ASoC: apple: Add A8 (t7000) MCA driver with PIO
 playback

The A8 has no DMA engine in the audio path: iOS lets the SmartIO
coprocessor memcpy PCM into a small SRAM FIFO ("shim") that hardware
drains into the MCA. Do the same from the AP with an hrtimer, so the SIO
firmware is not needed.

Supports what was verified on the iPhone 6 speaker: MCA as clock master,
48 kHz, S16_LE mono in slot 0 of an 8 x 16-bit frame.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
